{"type":"bullets","design":"S_001","title":"Defined scope of the Vertex AI agent deployment","lead":"The deployment establishes clear boundaries across priority queues, content corpora, agent workspaces and safety guardrails.","points":["In-scope call and chat queues: Covers reservation, baggage, MileagePlus, and disruption queues across Cisco Webex and Agent on Demand channels.","Grounded knowledge base boundaries: Indexes verified United standard operating procedures and fare rules, excluding external web sources.","Agent workspace rollout: Deploys inside existing Cisco Webex agent desktops across voice and digital teams in phased operational waves.","Safety guardrails: Enforces grounded citations for every suggestion while redacting payment cards and passenger personal data before model inference.","Out-of-scope items: Passenger service system changes and customer-facing voice bots are excluded."],"callout":{"label":"Scope focus","title":"Targeted rollout across high-impact contact queues","text":"Focusing the deployment on reservation, disruption and Agent on Demand workflows embeds Vertex AI Agent Assist directly into Cisco Webex desktops, giving frontline care teams verified policy answers and automated call summaries without altering core booking databases."},"notes":"This slide defines the operational and technical boundaries for the Vertex AI Agent Assist implementation at United Airlines. The scope targets high-volume voice and digital queues running on the Cisco Webex infrastructure and Agent on Demand touchpoints. By indexing only verified internal policies in Vertex AI Search and keeping legacy passenger service system replacements out of scope, the team reduces delivery risk and accelerates frontline adoption.

