{"type":"bullets","design":"S_001","title":"Governance boundaries and operational assumptions","lead":"Strict tenant boundaries protect passenger data while excluding legacy manual channels from the initial deployment.","points":["Data isolation: Vertex AI Search indexes only approved United policies within a dedicated Google Cloud tenant.","Zero external model training: passenger records and live transcripts never leave United security perimeters.","Out-of-scope channels: paper correspondence, airport ticket counters and manual back-office queues remain excluded.","Core telephony baseline: United maintains stable Cisco Webex audio streaming into Google Cloud."],"callout":{"label":"Primary governance focus","title":"Dedicated Google Cloud data isolation","text":"All generative responses are grounded strictly in approved United operational manuals using Vertex AI Search. Passenger data and live Agent on Demand transcripts remain isolated inside United virtual private cloud perimeters and never train external models. VPC Service Controls enforce tight data perimeters, while automated redaction strips sensitive information before queries reach indexing pipelines."},"notes":"This slide defines the governance boundaries and operational assumptions for the deployment. All Vertex AI capabilities operate within a dedicated Google Cloud boundary, grounded exclusively in approved United Airlines documentation without training external models. Manual back-office queues and physical airport counter workflows are excluded so the team stays focused on voice and digital Agent on Demand touchpoints integrated with Cisco Webex.

